      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "RulzTrainer likeness scoring: the trainer's own face / body scores on any images.\n\nReferences (what the person looks like)\n- Connect a reference image (or a batch), or type image files / folders into reference_paths, one per line.\n- For separate face and body references use face_paths / body_paths (or the face_images / body_images inputs). They replace the shared references for that score.\n\nImages to score\n- Connect an image (or a batch), and/or type files / folders into image_paths on the Score node.\n\nScale (the trainer's defaults)\n- 0 = what a stranger scores, 100 = what a typical reference scores against the others (2+ references needed for a measured 100, else a default).\n- baseline_paths / baseline_images: images from the base model without the LoRA set the 0, like the trainer's step-0 probe.\n- trainer_run: a RulzTrainer job folder uses that run's exact scale.\n\nResults\n- Summary: the averages (overall, face, body). Details: every image.\n- Turn on export_spreadsheet on the Export node for an .xlsx (Summary, Images, References sheets) or CSV files in ComfyUI's output folder.\n\nPaths are as this ComfyUI sees them: a ComfyUI in WSL reads C:\\ai as /mnt/c/ai."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "RulzTrainer likeness scoring: the trainer's own face / body scores on any images.\n\nReferences (what the person looks like)\n- Connect a reference image (or a batch), or type image files / folders into reference_paths, one per line.\n- For separate face and body references use face_paths / body_paths (or the face_images / body_images inputs). They replace the shared references for that score.\n\nImages to score\n- Connect an image (or a batch), and/or type files / folders into image_paths on the Score node.\n\nScale (the trainer's defaults)\n- 0 = what a stranger scores, 100 = what a typical reference scores against the others (2+ references needed for a measured 100, else a default).\n- baseline_paths / baseline_images: images from the base model without the LoRA set the 0, like the trainer's step-0 probe.\n- trainer_run: a RulzTrainer job folder uses that run's exact scale.\n\nResults\n- Summary: the averages (overall, face, body). Details: every image.\n- Turn on export_spreadsheet on the Export node for an .xlsx (Summary, Images, References sheets) or CSV files in ComfyUI's output folder.\n\nPaths are as this ComfyUI sees them: a ComfyUI in WSL reads C:\\ai as /mnt/c/ai."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
